/-!
# Recognizing complete intersection homomorphisms from a good factorization

Let `A → S → B` be a factorization of a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings with `S → B`
surjective, `A → S` flat and `S / 𝔪_A S` a regular local ring.  Then the kernel of `S → B` is
generated by a regular sequence exactly when the induced homomorphism `A^ → B^` between the
maximal-ideal-adic completions is a complete intersection homomorphism.

Completing the whole factorization gives a good factorization `A^ → S^ → B^`: completion
preserves flatness, surjectivity and the Noetherian local property, and the closed fibre of
`A^ → S^` is the completion of `S / 𝔪_A S`, hence still regular.  The kernel of `S^ → B^` is the
extension of `ker(S → B)` along the faithfully flat map `S → S^`, so a regular sequence
generating one ideal is carried to the other: upwards directly, and downwards by faithfully flat
descent of Koszul-regularity.  Finally `S^` is replaced by an isomorphic ring in the universe
where `IsCompleteIntersectionHom` quantifies, which is possible because the completion of a
Noetherian local ring injects into the product of its finite-length quotients.

## Main results

* `LocalCompleteIntersection.isGeneratedByRegularSequence_ker_iff_isCompleteIntersectionHom`: the
  regular-sequence criterion for a good factorization.

## Implementation notes

The map on completions is `adicCompletionMap` specialized to the maximal ideals, and the
hypotheses describing the displayed diagram are packaged by `IsGoodFactorization`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09QD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09QD)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace LocalCompleteIntersection

universe u v w

